      "sha": "a90c6e8d072558d07683c6586bb922ec8253db6c",
      "message": "fix: config.ini duration default values / fix SENDMAIL_TIMEOUT default (#14828)\n\nSince f8fc5b9daff5f591a2c88011657e251ce5de9fb6 / #10273 the default value for a duration ini key was no longer written to the value for the \"empty\" case, such that after\n\n```\n  sec.Key(\"VALUE\").MustDuration(defaultValue)\n```\n\nthe value would remain empty if it was empty to begin with.\n\nBecause we have no access to the private value field from `ini.Key`, we call `MustDuration()` on it. Compare https://github.com/go-ini/ini/blob/v1.67.3/key.go#L332C3-L332C35\n\nI reviewed the mentioned commit and, luckily, `[mailer] SENDMAIL_TIMEOUT` is the only affected ini key, because in all other cases, the return value of `MustDuration()` is assigned to the configuration field directly.\n\nFixes #14635\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14828\nReviewed-by: Andreas Ahlenstorf <redacted@example.invalid>\nReviewed-by: Gusted <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
      "author": {
